While diving deeper into DevOps & Cloud, one concept I keep coming back to is the Client-Server model — the foundation of how most modern systems communicate.

Here’s the idea in simple terms:

🔹𝐂𝐥𝐢𝐞𝐧𝐭 → Makes the request (browser, mobile app, or any device).

🔹𝐒𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐞𝐫 → Processes the request and sends back a response (data, web page, file, etc.).

A simple analogy:

 🧑 Client = You placing an order at a restaurant

 👨🍳 Server = The kitchen preparing and serving your dish

✅𝐖𝐡𝐲 𝐢𝐬 𝐭𝐡𝐢𝐬 𝐢𝐦𝐩𝐨𝐫𝐭𝐚𝐧𝐭?

✨ Because everything we do in DevOps — from managing APIs and deploying apps to scaling microservices — relies on this fundamental architecture.

